Minimalist Image Director System Manual
Step 1: Define the Emotional Target
Every deployment profile must isolate its quadrant boundaries: Warm vs Cold, Active vs Calm.

Target Mapping Rules
Warm Pink (#FFC0CB): Nurturing gentleness (Child development).

Terracotta (#C2704F): Earthy warmth, trust, and structural permanence (Family/Wellness).

Cream/Ivory (#FAF8F5): Soft, high-comfort background canvas layers.

Step 2: Build the 4-Layer Prompt Architecture
Layer 1: Style Prefix (Strict Template Suffix)
Plaintext
Warm minimalist photography. Soft natural light, shallow depth of field, [BRAND PALETTE TONES]. 
Candid moment, not posed. Shot on 85mm f/1.8 lens, Kodak Portra 400 film look, natural skin texture. 
No text, no logos, no watermarks. Warm color temperature.
Layer 2: Body Language Controls
Enforce positive Duchenne smile configurations, alignment at eye levels, relaxed cross-arm exemptions, and physical touch indicators.

Layer 3: Target Emotion Descriptors
Map visual outcomes strictly via target terms: "pure delight", "deeply focused", "gentle touch", "suspended possibility".

Layer 4: Anti-Pattern Blockers
Append negative strings to suppress cold outputs:

Plaintext
--no plastic skin, glossy surfaces, artificial lighting, airbrushed, sterile, clinical, 3D render, CGI, harsh shadows, cool tones
